  "comment": "**What it does**\nFinds companies **steadily shrinking their own share count with real cash** -\nthe net-buyback signal (research: share reduction predicts returns; dividends\nalone barely do).\n- **The signal** - share count DOWN 3%+ over the last year (the brief said\n  ~2%+; 3% keeps the list focused - loosen to -2 for more names). Net of\n  stock-comp: a \"buyback program\" eaten by new grants doesn't pass.\n- **Funded properly** - free-cash-flow margin 5%+, ROIC 8%+, debt under\n  control (debt-free companies aren't punished for missing debt data).\n- **Profitable only.** $1B and bigger.\n\n**How to tweak**\n- More names? Share shrink to -1, or `fcf_margin` to 3.\n- Cannibals only? Share shrink to -4 (the Munger \"cannibals\" cut).\n\n**How to sort for best picks**\n- **Sort by `quality_score`**, tiebreak `value_score` (buybacks at low\n  prices compound hardest).\n- The raw `share_count_chg_1y` column sorted ascending shows the most\n  aggressive shrinkers first.",
  "ai_instructions": "Find companies steadily shrinking their own share count with real cash \u2014 the\nnet-buyback signal (quietly one of the best-evidenced return signals; dividends\nalone predict little, buybacks do).\n- **Goal**: shareholder-yield quality. **Dividends**: nice but not required.\n- **The signal**: share count DOWN at least ~2% over the last year \u2014 real net\n  buybacks, not buybacks eaten by stock-comp dilution.\n- **Funded properly**: healthy free-cash-flow margin and solid returns on capital;\n  debt under control (don't punish debt-free companies for missing debt data).\n- **Profitable companies only.** **Size**: $1B and bigger. **Kinds**: normal\n  stocks only. **Risk**: moderate.\n- **Results**: ~30-150 names. **Sorting**: quality first, tiebreak value.",
